  "finding": "Same native tool/thread/turn: admitted pre-hook returned, commandExecution completed exit0 arrived with row reserved, evaluator set toolCoverage false and stopped its ledger before post-hook. Later pre-hooks all recorded the stop; the two post-hooks eventually settled. No prior stop/deadline at the first completion. This confirms a completion/post ordering defect in evaluator, not OpenClaw task quality or unavailable authorization.",
  "unknowns": [
    "Whole three-turn composition did not complete",
    "Native physical cleanup not confirmed",
    "Exact reason the ordinary actor did not return before public controller deadline",
    "Original quality comparison not run"
  ],
  "proposedSmallCorrection": "For an admitted exec in the exact native thread and turn, accept completed commandExecution with integer exit code as dispatch and settlement evidence before post; retain terminal status/exit; later post is idempotent. Unknown/cancelled/mismatched/nonterminal identities still stop. No native cleanup promotion or admission/profile change.",
